From: Patrik Eriksson <patrik.m.eriksson@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:27:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] scripts: APERTAR_RT=1 runs Core under SCHED_FIFO on cores
 1-3 like cinepi-raw; README knob table

Why: cinemate starts cinepi-raw with chrt -f 70, ionice -c2 -n0 and taskset -c 1-3 (its
LimitRTPRIO=80 unit), while Core relies on a nice -5 boost of the callback thread. Scheduling
parity was plan row 5 of the drop-frames project; the kb's research (working/dng-chain, R2, R7,
verified in V/H15) keeps it as an A/B instrument, not a default: whole-process FIFO is the wrong
shape for Core (equal-priority FIFO threads never preempt each other, so the capture thread can
wait behind FIFO writers), and the expected scheduling delay under the current nice -5 is tens
to hundreds of microseconds.

What: the start script prefixes the exec with chrt/ionice/taskset when APERTAR_RT=1 and chrt
is permitted (APERTAR_RT_PRIORITY, APERTAR_RT_CPUS adjust it; an empty APERTAR_RT_CPUS skips the
pinning), otherwise logs one line and starts as before. The capture-priority drop-in gains
LimitRTPRIO=80, unused without APERTAR_RT=1. The README gets a table of the write-path knobs
for A/B tests and the updated trim sentence.

Tested: bash -n; the script run with a stand-in binary both with APERTAR_RT=1 (prefix logged) and
without (plain exec). Reviewed (V/PATCHES.md): the empty-array expansion and the ${VAR-default}
form behave under set -euo pipefail. Not run on the Pi.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
